# Logitech G915 (046d:c33e) vendor HID++ interface -> uaccess for the seat user.
#
# Scoped to USB interface 02 deliberately. Interfaces 00 and 01 are the
# keystroke interfaces; granting the logged-in user read access to their hidraw
# nodes would be a keylogger surface. Interface 02 is the vendor collection
# (usage page 0xFF00) and carries no keystroke reports.
#
# Matched on properties rather than sysfs attributes. bInterfaceNumber lives on
# the USB interface (3-6:1.2) while idVendor/idProduct live on the USB device
# (3-6), and udev requires every ATTRS key in one rule to match the same parent
# device -- so ATTRS{idVendor} + ATTRS{bInterfaceNumber} can never match. The
# ID_* properties below are set on the hidraw device itself by udev's usb_id
# builtin, which 60-persistent-hidraw.rules imports, well before this file is
# read.
#
# install.sh puts this in /usr/local/lib/udev/rules.d/; the .deb puts it in
# /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/. Either way, reload with:
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   sudo udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw --action=add
# Triggering the usb subsystem does not re-run hidraw rules.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c33e", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"

# The same keyboard, through its LIGHTSPEED receiver (046d:c541).
#
# Read off the hardware on 2026-09-22. This receiver does not give a paired
# device a hidraw node of its own the way the mouse's c547 does: it presents
# only its own three interfaces, and the keyboard's traffic comes over them.
# The layout is the same as a cabled device's, verified from the report
# descriptors: 00 is a pointer collection, 01 is the keyboard collection that
# carries keystrokes, and 02 is the vendor HID++ collection at usage page
# 0xFF00. So the scoping is the same as the cable's, and for the same reason.
#
# A receiver's vendor interface carries the HID++ traffic of everything
# paired to it. Keystrokes are not on it: those are interface 01, which gets
# nothing.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c541", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
